{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261026T033809Z-8b4770e1", "ts": "2026-10-26T03:42:21Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.0-dev", "branch": "feature/733-consumer-digest"}, "body": {"base_commit": "0964afa10cdadf2de03264ab992330914cb50ff3", "base_tree": "369680aed02723463401e3e24f58c1ce62079c42", "head_tree": "42a48f23b152cfe1c9869c40c1582676cc99ab02", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "94f08b4a811c862e4128f92e31dd2ff6088d177d", "mode": "chunk (lighter pass, not ready for push)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "inner", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5[1m]"}], "files_reviewed": ["documentation/issues/733-design.md", "documentation/issues/733-requirements.md"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-consumer-digest.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/release-plan-v3.8.0.md", ".prawduct/changes/consumer-digest.md", "documentation/issues/733-design.md", "documentation/issues/733-requirements.md"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-consumer-digest.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/release-plan-v3.8.0.md", ".prawduct/changes/consumer-digest.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "blocking", "title": "CD8 'already archived' is keyed on scope, so a same-scope fragment added after the cut is silently deleted", "recommendation": "instance. Why: Section 6 step 2 decides 'this fragment's archive entry exists' by scopes_tagged_for (scope= + release= tags), and scope is a reused identifier. A fragment written for the same scope after the cut (a follow-up on the same branch scope) lands in cleanup, so it is unlinked without being archived or published. CD8's second bullet requires that fragment to refuse release-already-cut, and today's cut does not lose it, because _compose_bucket dedupes by Block.key (entry content). Fix: decide 'already archived' by the archive's own identity: render_entry(fragment, release=version) gives a block whose key is present in the archive. Anything else refuses release-already-cut. Add a re-run table row and a test-plan case: same scope, new content after the cut, refuses.", "files": ["documentation/issues/733-design.md"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "blocking", "title": "CD8 completion is unreachable through the stated control flow (lingering headline, cleanup-only runs)", "recommendation": "instance. Why: Section 6 keeps plan_cut's early returns ('an empty cut returns early', and `if not cut: return result`) ahead of step 2. cut_cmd also returns 'nothing to do' at `if not cut_plan.cut` before apply_cut. So re-run table row 4 never runs: no fragments left, headline file lingering after a removal failure on the headline unlink. The stale headline then survives into the next release, which passes no-headline and publishes the previous release's headline. Row 2 also works only if cleanup fragments stay in `cut`, and the design does not say whether they do. If they move out, cut_cmd prints 'nothing to do' and removes nothing. Fix: state that the release-file check runs before the empty-cut returns, and that cut_cmd applies whenever cleanup or headline_file is non-empty. Pin rows 2 and 4 in the test plan. Also decide whether the lingering-headline removal must avoid deleting a NEXT release's headline already written there, for example by removing it only when its text equals the release file's headline paragraph.", "files": ["documentation/issues/733-design.md"], "fid": "R-2"}], "counts": {"blocking": 2, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Suffix-insensitive release-in-changelog blocks products that cut prereleases", "recommendation": "RELEASE_VALUE_RE admits prereleases, so a product can cut v1.4.0-rc.1, which inserts `## [1.4.0-rc.1]`. names_release then drops the suffix on both sides, so every later cut of v1.4.0 or rc.2 refuses release-in-changelog until the shipped rc section is deleted by hand. This comes from CD7's wording ('any prerelease suffix included'), which was written for prawduct's -dev section. Disposition default ACCEPT; if a product cuts prereleases, narrow the match, for example by treating only `-dev` headings as an unreleased marker.", "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Golden starting state: plan's `## v9.9.9-dev.1` fixture vs CD11's renamed `## vX.Y.Z`", "recommendation": "Today's cut does not rename. A fixture whose section is `## v9.9.9-dev.1`, cut as v9.9.9, captures that heading, and the new flow writes `## v9.9.9`, so the pair cannot be byte-equal. The design's CD11 test row does not pin the starting state. Name it in the design's test plan (section `## v9.9.9` + headline, `--release v9.9.9`) so Chunk 02 captures the state CD11 describes.", "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "write_all_or_none rollback restores priors via read_text (universal newlines)", "recommendation": "The Chunk 02 constraint covers only the forward write. The prior captured for rollback is read with path.read_text, which turns CRLF into LF, so a restored CRLF changelog would come back re-line-ended. This is safe today only because the changelog is the last write. Either extend the constraint to priors (capture bytes), or state that the changelog write is last. Batch into Chunk 02.", "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Phase 0's 'VERSION fallback the call site can compute cheaply' is vague and prawduct-pathed", "recommendation": "NOTE. _resolve_version's fallback reads plugin/VERSION, and per its own docstring it is a guessed-low -dev marker, so the early release-in-changelog check may test the wrong release. Say exactly which value is passed, or pass only --release.", "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Blank-line 'Before' rule at index 0 unspecified", "recommendation": "NOTE. When the first line is the version heading, nothing precedes the insert. State that no blank line is added at index 0 (after the BOM).", "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "record-lint change-fragment: empty-narrative and empty-consumer-note in .prawduct/changes/consumer-digest.md", "recommendation": "WARNING at the boundary. Chunk 07's deliverable writes both, so ACCEPT here.", "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Requirement amendments A1-A4 are not marked owner-vetoable", "recommendation": "NOTE. They are recorded in the design and inline in the requirements, but unlike Decision 8 they are not tagged 'inferred, owner can veto'. A4 retires a check. Mark them when committing.", "oid": "O-7"}], "duration_seconds": 600, "scope": "consumer-digest", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": "369680aed02723463401e3e24f58c1ce62079c42", "chunks": ["01"], "chunks_proposed": ["07"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-consumer-digest.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/release-plan-v3.8.0.md", ".prawduct/changes/consumer-digest.md", "documentation/issues/733-design.md", "documentation/issues/733-requirements.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-consumer-digest.md", "findings": [{"check": "change-fragment", "path": ".prawduct/changes/consumer-digest.md", "line": null, "detail": "empty-narrative: say what changed and why above the consumer note"}, {"check": "change-fragment", "path": ".prawduct/changes/consumer-digest.md", "line": null, "detail": "empty-consumer-note: write the note, or `none: <reason>` when there is nothing to tell consumers"}], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0